            "is_markdown": false,
            "bug_id": 19287,
            "text": "readRDS() and unserialize() can seg.fault, or return garbage, on a serialized ALTREP object of one of the base classes whose state has the wrong shape.\n\nReproducible example: attached as altrep-unserialize-state-repro.R; every case should signal an error, but in R 4.6.1 two return garbage and three seg.fault, the last being OSS-Fuzz testcase 6358277886377984 (111 bytes, read with readRDS()).\n\nAnalysis: the Unserialize methods in src/main/altclasses.c (compact sequences, wrappers, deferred strings, mmap) take the state apart without checking its type or length. CAR() of an external pointer state is a NULL address, CAR() of a plain vector is its length, and short vectors are read past their end.\n\nProposed patch: attached as altrep-unserialize-state.diff, against r90844. It checks the state in all five methods and signals \"invalid ... serialized state\"; the added test in tests/reg-tests-1e.R fails without it. It supersedes attachment 3842 on the closed bug 19047, which covered only the compact sequences and was not applied. As there, this is a robustness fix, since unserializing untrusted data is documented as unsafe.\n\nThe patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/336, where CI results can be seen."
          },
          {
