            "creator": "kevinushey",
            "bug_id": 19287,
            "text": "Created attachment 4012\nR-exts: ALTREP Unserialize methods should check their state\n\nI've attached a separate documentation patch for Writing R Extensions. To find a class that is not registered yet, unserialize() loads the namespace of the package named in the stream, so a malformed state can reach any installed package's ALTREP class, which the code fix in attachment 4010 cannot protect. The added sentences, next to the description of how a class is identified, ask Unserialize and UnserializeEX methods to check the state's type and length and signal an error. The patch also fixes a stray comma there.\n\nIt applies independently of attachment 4010 and of the R-exts patch on bug 19227. Patch also at https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/336",
            "is_markdown": false,
